/*.log

node_modules/

/plugin_dev.lua

# User customizations — personal plugin files, never tracked. No stub is
# committed: lua/custom/ is outside lua/yoda/, so a tracked file would ship
# a generic `custom.*` module to every consumer's runtimepath.
/lua/custom/

# Benchmark temporary files
benchmarks/temp/

# Test coverage output
coverage/


# Task tracking (local only). The /TODO.md exception that lived here covered
# the v1.0.0 restructure handoff doc, which was removed once the migration
# completed — without dropping the negation, a fresh session TODO.md at the
# repo root would be tracked again.
**/TODO.md

# Lock file written by Neovim's built-in vim.pack. Machine-specific: it
# records absolute paths to local plugin checkouts. yoda uses lazy.nvim, so
# this only appears when experimenting with vim.pack in a local session.
/nvim-pack-lock.json
